## Gov Metrics field test — iteration 2

Cave Pony reviewed the active evidence-page discoverability PR rather than starting a new feature.

## Finding

- upstream retrieval time was published as Dataset/RSS `dateModified`;
- RSS `<lastBuildDate>` used the wall clock, so unchanged evidence produced different output;
- a stale test froze one exact steering sentence instead of the durable public-money accountability intent.

## Cave Pony improvement

- require every field, label and claim to come from the event or authority it names;
- keep observation, publication, retrieval, validation, build and display times separate;
- require deterministic generated output when inputs are unchanged;
- reject wall-clock, randomness, unstable ordering and environment-specific output without a present need;
- test behaviour and semantic invariants rather than incidental prose or implementation shape;
- add these failure classes to audit mode.

## Proof

- focused contract tests added in `tests/test_semantic_contract.py`;
- field evidence recorded in `benchmarks/field-tests/2026-07-19-gov-metrics-iteration-2.md`;
- related application correction is on wilfgrainger/gov-metrics#255;
- comparative model benchmark remains explicitly not run.

## Root cause

The shared stagedJson contract correctly normalizes a single branch object into a one-item branch array for internal processing. The enrichment engine then returned that canonical array directly, so an object-root source no longer failed with `Could not locate stagedJson node at 0`, but its exported root shape silently changed from object to array.

## Change

- retain canonical branch-array processing internally;
- record whether the accepted source was a single branch object;
- restore that single-object shape only after enrichment and geometry validation;
- keep bare-array and managed-stage envelope behavior unchanged;
- block export if a single object unexpectedly normalizes to anything other than one root branch.

## Regression coverage

A focused Node test proves that both direct-object and JSON-string object roots:

- enrich the root branch and nested components;
- remain objects rather than arrays;
- preserve source attributes and geometry;
- resolve component weight and dimensional evidence;
- do not mutate the input object.

The existing 1885 fixture workflow runs this regression before the deterministic fixture and topology tests.

## Scope

Exactly three files:

- `tabs/xml-cii-2019-standalone/stagedjson-enrichment/stagedjson-enrichment-engine.js`
- `tests/stagedjson-object-root-shape.test.js`
- `.github/workflows/stagedjson-1885-fixture-reproducibility.yml`

## Validation

Green on head `6796351e4c5a4bd71a7129340e87fbbe41cbcfce`:

- `1885 StagedJSON Fixture Reproducibility` run #31 — success;
- `XML CII Standalone Mission 01` run #166 — success;
- `PSI116 TopoFix Standalone Integration` run #15 — success.

