Follow-up to #60638. That PR gave `@hermes/plugin-sdk` a real surface (`ctx.rest`, `ctx.socket`, `ctx.storage`, the UI kit) and explicitly **deferred plugin-scoped i18n** — the one door a runtime/third-party plugin needs so it isn't forced to edit core `en.ts` to ship translated copy. This adds that door, scoped exactly like `ctx.storage`.

## The door

A plugin registers its own locale bundles under its id and reads them back with a scoped translator. It never touches the core catalog.

```js
export default {
  id: 'cost-meter',
  register(ctx) {
    ctx.i18n.register({
      en: { title: 'Cost', spent: n => `$${n} spent` },
      ja: { title: 'コスト', spent: n => `$${n} 使用` }
    })
    // ...
  }
}

// in a component
const t = usePluginI18n('cost-meter')
t('spent', 42) // follows the app's active locale
```

## How it mirrors the existing SDK

- **Namespaced like `ctx.storage`.** Bundles live under the plugin id; plugins can't read or clobber each other's (or core's) strings.
- **Follows the app locale, doesn't own it.** Resolution is `display.language` → the plugin's own `en` → the raw key. Plugins never persist their own locale (per the desktop authority rule: the backend owns anything another surface can change).
- **Same lifecycle.** `ctx.i18n.register` returns a disposer the loader tracks like `register`/`socket`; a plugin's bundles are torn down on unload/reload.
- **Symmetric consumers, like core.** `usePluginI18n(id)` for React UI (re-renders on a locale switch or a late registration); `ctx.i18n.t` (module-level) for handlers/stores — mirroring `useI18n` / `translateNow`.
- **Free reach to runtime plugins.** The SDK runtime shim re-exports the barrel, so disk/third-party plugins get the identical surface as bundled ones — no wiring.

## Footprint

No new core strings, no new model tools, no config, no prompt-cache impact. Rather than fork the resolver, the core `active → English → key` fallback is lifted out of `translateNow` into a single shared `translateFrom(source, locale, …)` that both the app catalog and plugin bundles resolve through — one policy, one home.

## Test plan

- [x] `npm run typecheck` (desktop) — clean
- [x] `eslint` on all touched files — clean
- [x] `vitest run src/i18n src/contrib` — 27 passed, incl. new `plugin-i18n.test.tsx` covering the fallback chain, per-plugin scoping, merge + dispose, `ctx.i18n.t` runtime-locale read, and `usePluginI18n` reactivity (locale switch + late registration)

